solution:
const { chromium } = require('playwright');
(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto('http://localhost:5000/pages/level-02/');
  await page.locator('#reveal-btn').click();
  const msg = await page.locator('#secret-message').textContent();
  if (msg && msg.includes('Playwright rocks')) console.log('LEVEL_PASSED');
  await browser.close();
})();

explanation:
`locator.click()` simulates a real mouse click on an element. After clicking, use another locator to check the result.

```
await page.locator('#reveal-btn').click();
const msg = await page.locator('#secret-message').textContent();
if (msg.includes('Playwright rocks')) console.log('LEVEL_PASSED');
```

Playwright automatically waits for the element to be visible and stable before clicking — no manual `waitForSelector` needed.

