solution:
const { chromium } = require('playwright');
(async () => {
  const browser = await chromium.launch();
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto('http://localhost:5000/pages/level-03/');
  await page.locator('#username').fill('wizard');
  await page.locator('#password').fill('playwright123');
  await page.locator('#login-btn').click();
  const success = page.locator('#success-message');
  await success.waitFor({ state: 'visible' });
  console.log('LEVEL_PASSED');
  await browser.close();
})();

explanation:
`locator.fill(value)` clears an input and types the given text. Use it for text fields, email inputs, and textareas.

After filling, click the submit button or press Enter:

```
await page.locator('#username').fill('wizard');
await page.locator('#password').fill('playwright123');
await page.locator('#login-btn').click();
// wait for success
const success = page.locator('#success-message');
await success.waitFor({ state: 'visible' });
```

`waitFor({ state: 'visible' })` pauses until the element appears — useful after form submission.

